  "articleBody": "Restoration remodeling can be tricky, and it's easy to stumble into some common mistakes. One of the biggest is underestimating the scope of the project. It’s vital to define your budget and deadlines early on to avoid surprises down the line. Another frequent misstep? Not clarifying how change orders will be handled. Trust me, things can come up once work begins, so having a clear process for those changes saves a lot of headaches. Don't forget about lead times for materials or insurance review either; these can really impact your timeline. To avoid these issues, look for a contractor who offers an itemized estimate and has a clear change-order process. It's also super helpful to ask about their experience with similar projects and how they track the schedule. A good pro will also be transparent about warranties. When you’re dealing with an insurance claim, or if there’s hidden damage, structural issues, or permits involved, bringing in a qualified remodeler like HH Remodeling LLC early on can make all the difference. We’re here to make your house feel more like a home, and part of that is helping you navigate these complexities.",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-09"
